# Keeps `railway up` uploads small for this monorepo -- every service's
# Dockerfile only COPYs its own `services/<name>/` subtree (confirmed
# against infra/docker/*.Dockerfile), so none of the paths below are ever
# part of a real build context. Without this, a `railway up` run from the
# repo root uploads local dependency caches, build output, and data
# directories that can individually run into the hundreds of MB -- real,
# hit live 2026-08-21: a forecast-api deploy failed outright with a 413
# Payload Too Large once the ingestion service's local staging data grew
# past ~230MB combined.
node_modules/
.venv/
.next/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Per-service local data/notebook-output directories -- real ingested
# data, trained-model artifacts, and notebook scratch output, none of it
# needed by any service's Docker build (each Dockerfile COPYs source
# code, not these).
services/ingestion/data/
services/forecast-api/mlruns/
services/forecast-api/notebooks/*.zip
services/forecast-api/notebooks/lstm_demand_onnx_bundle/
services/forecast-api/mlflow.db

# Stray root-level DuckDB temp files (hundreds of small per-connection
# copies observed live under `data/staging/` at the repo root, unrelated
# to any service's own `data/` directory) -- not real source either way.
/data/
